{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When the Most High gave nations their inheritance.</b> That He gave each and every nation its inheritance." "<b>When He separated the children of man.</b> In the generation of the Dispersion, when He separated them and scattered them and each man went to his place, as it is said: ״ויפץ א׳ אותם משם וגו׳״." "<b>He established the borders of the peoples according to the number of the children of Israel.</b> He designated an inheritance for the twelve tribes even though they were not yet born — how so? He delivered the land of Israel to the children of Canaan, who are servants to the children of Shem, so that they would not be able to contest when they come to take it from their hand. And the children of Canaan were twelve, as it is written: ״וכנען ילד את צידון בכורו ואת חת ואת היבוסי ואת האמורי ואת הגרגשי ואת החוי ואת הערקי ואת הסיני ואת הארודי ואת הצמרי ואת החמתי״ — that is eleven. And it is written: ״ואחר נפוצו משפחות הכנעני״, which implies that one of the families split into two — that is the Perizite, who is not enumerated here — that is twelve. And this is 'according to the number of the children of Israel.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:45.595673233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}